<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lothian</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lothian is the region of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/firth-of-forth">Firth of Forth</a> and the Lammermuir Hills, around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edinburgh">Edinburgh</a>. Home of the Votadini and the British kingdom of Gododdin, it was conquered by Northumbria in the 7th century and passed to the kings of Scots in the 10th and early 11th centuries, a gain secured after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-carham">Battle of Carham</a> around 1018.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lothian.jpg" alt="Lothian" width="320" height="482" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Brythones, derivative of Visitor from Wikishire · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lothian_County.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
